      "left": {
        "pageNumber": 11,
        "runningHead": "CH. 6 • RISK FORMULA & CVE VS CWE",
        "content": "<div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Vulnerability Assessment Scope:</strong> A <strong>Vulnerability Assessment (VA)</strong> identifies, catalogs, and ranks vulnerabilities using automated tools <strong>WITHOUT</strong> actively exploiting them.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Chapter 6 • Vulnerability Management & Standards</span>\n      <h2>Vulnerability vs Weakness & The Fundamental Risk Formula</h2>\n    </div>\n    <p>Effective security governance begins with formal definitions of risk and software flaws:</p>\n\n    <h3>The Fundamental Mathematical Risk Equation</h3>\n    <div class=\"analogy-box\">\n      <strong>Risk Equation:</strong> <code>Risk = Threat × Vulnerability × Impact</code><br>\n      • <strong>Threat:</strong> Any circumstance, adversary, or event with the potential to adversely impact an asset;<br>\n      • <strong>Vulnerability:</strong> A flaw, weakness, or software bug that can be exploited by a threat;<br>\n      • <strong>Impact:</strong> The magnitude of harm or monetary loss resulting from successful exploitation.\n    </div>\n\n    <h3>Vulnerability vs Weakness (CVE vs CWE)</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Weakness (CWE / Common Weakness Enumeration):</strong> A conceptual flaw or coding bug in software design, implementation, or architecture (e.g. CWE-89: SQL Injection, CWE-79: Cross-Site Scripting).</li>\n      <li><strong>Vulnerability (CVE / Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures):</strong> A specific instance of a weakness occurring within a distinct software product or binary version that enables real-world compromise (e.g. CVE-2021-44228: Apache Log4j RCE). Managed by MITRE and the National Vulnerability Database (NVD).</li>\n    </ul>"
      },
      "right": {
        "pageNumber": 12,
        "runningHead": "CVSS V3.1 BASE METRICS & RATINGS",
        "content": "<div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">CVSS v3.1 Architecture</span>\n      <h2>Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS v3.1) Metrics</h2>\n    </div>\n    <p>CVSS v3.1 evaluates severity across three metric groups producing scores from 0.0 to 10.0:</p>\n\n    <h3>Base Metric Vector Metrics</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Exploitability Metrics:</strong>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Attack Vector (AV):</strong> Network (N), Adjacent (A), Local (L), Physical (P);</li>\n          <li><strong>Attack Complexity (AC):</strong> Low (L), High (H);</li>\n          <li><strong>Privileges Required (PR):</strong> None (N), Low (L), High (H);</li>\n          <li><strong>User Interaction (UI):</strong> None (N), Required (R).</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li><strong>Scope (S):</strong> Unchanged (U) vs Changed (C). If an exploit in one component impacts resources beyond its security boundary (e.g. virtual machine escape), Scope is <strong>Changed (C)</strong>.</li>\n      <li><strong>Impact Metrics:</strong> Confidentiality (C), Integrity (I), Availability (A) — None (N), Low (L), High (H).</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <table class=\"statutory-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr><th>CVSS v3.1 Score</th><th>Severity Rating</th><th>Remediation SLA</th></tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><strong>0.0</strong></td><td>None</td><td>No action needed</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>0.1 – 3.9</strong></td><td>Low</td><td>Next maintenance cycle</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>4.0 – 6.9</strong></td><td>Medium</td><td>30 to 60 days</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>7.0 – 8.9</strong></td><td>High</td><td>7 to 14 days</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>9.0 – 10.0</strong></td><td>Critical</td><td>Immediate emergency patch (24-48 hours)</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Exam Rule on Risk & CVSS:</strong> <code>Risk = Threat × Vulnerability × Impact</code>. <strong>CWE</strong> defines general flaw types; <strong>CVE</strong> catalogs specific real-world flaws. A score of <strong>9.0–10.0 is Critical</strong>. <strong>Scope Changed (S:C)</strong> indicates cross-boundary impact (e.g., hypervisor escapes).\n    </div>\n\n    \n    \n        <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-banner\">\n          <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-info\">\n            <span style=\"font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 8px;\">🎯</span>\n            <div>\n              <strong style=\"font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--text-heading);\">Test Your Mastery: Spread 6</strong>\n              <div style=\"font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted);\">Practice all 10 targeted exam questions (Q51–Q60) on Vulnerability Management & CVSS v3.1.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button class=\"btn-tool btn-mcq\" onclick=\"window.openMCQForSpread(5)\" style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 6px 14px;\">Start Quiz (Q51–Q60) →</button>\n        </div>"
      }
