        "runningHead": "VA VS PT & RULES OF ENGAGEMENT",
        "content": "<div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Standards & Legal Agreements</span>\n      <h2>Vulnerability Assessment vs Pentest & Rules of Engagement</h2>\n    </div>\n    <h3>Vulnerability Assessment vs Penetration Testing</h3>\n    <table class=\"statutory-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Vulnerability Assessment (VA)</th><th>Penetration Testing (PT)</th></tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><strong>Primary Goal</strong></td><td>Comprehensive list of all known vulnerabilities across all assets.</td><td>Demonstrating whether a specific flaw can be exploited to breach security.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Methodology</strong></td><td>Automated scanners (Nessus, Qualys, OpenVAS) with banner grabbing.</td><td>Manual exploitation, chaining vulnerabilities, lateral movement.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Exploitation</strong></td><td>Does NOT exploit vulnerabilities; reports theoretical risk.</td><td>Actively exploits flaws to prove real-world business impact.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h3>Rules of Engagement (RoE) & NIST SP 800-115</h3>\n    <p>The <strong>Rules of Engagement (RoE)</strong> document establishes legal authorization (\"Get Out of Jail Free\" card), testing windows, forbidden targets, denial-of-service limitations, and communication protocols. <strong>NIST SP 800-115</strong> provides the official US federal Technical Guide to Information Security Testing and Assessment.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Exam Rule on Testing Frameworks:</strong> <strong>White Box</strong> gives full code and architecture access. <strong>PTES</strong> has <strong>7 distinct phases</strong>. <strong>VA</strong> identifies flaws using automated scanners without exploitation; <strong>PT</strong> actively exploits flaws. <strong>RoE</strong> provides legal authorization.\n    </div>\n\n    \n    \n        <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-banner\">\n          <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-info\">\n            <span style=\"font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 8px;\">🎯</span>\n            <div>\n              <strong style=\"font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--text-heading);\">Test Your Mastery: Spread 7</strong>\n              <div style=\"font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted);\">Practice all 10 targeted exam questions (Q61–Q70) on Pentest Methodologies & PTES Framework.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button class=\"btn-tool btn-mcq\" onclick=\"window.openMCQForSpread(6)\" style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 6px 14px;\">Start Quiz (Q61–Q70) →</button>\n        </div>"
