        "pageNumber": 28,
        "runningHead": "UNQUOTED SERVICE PATHS & MSIS",
        "content": "<div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Log4Shell, Dirty Pipe & Shellshock:</strong> <strong>Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228)</strong> in Apache Log4j executed remote code via <strong>JNDI</strong> injection.  <strong>Dirty Pipe (CVE-2022-0847)</strong> abuses uninitialized pipe buffer flags to overwrite read-only files. <strong>Shellshock (CVE-2014-6271)</strong> executes trailing commands in Bash environment functions. <strong>Clickjacking (UI Redressing)</strong> overlays an invisible iframe, defended via <strong>X-Frame-Options: DENY</strong>. <strong>MIME-Sniffing</strong> occurs when browsers override declared Content-Type headers on untrusted uploads, executing scripts unless prevented by <code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Windows Privilege Escalation</span>\n      <h2>Unquoted Service Paths & AlwaysInstallElevated</h2>\n    </div>\n    <h3>Windows Privilege Escalation Vectors</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Unquoted Service Paths:</strong> When a Windows service executable path containing spaces is stored without enclosing quotation marks (e.g., <code>C:\\Program Files\\My App\\service.exe</code>), Windows attempts to execute binaries in order:\n        <ol>\n          <li><code>C:\\Program.exe</code></li>\n          <li><code>C:\\Program Files\\My.exe</code></li>\n          <li><code>C:\\Program Files\\My App\\service.exe</code></li>\n        </ol>\n        If an unprivileged user has write access to <code>C:\\</code>, planting a malicious <code>Program.exe</code> grants SYSTEM execution upon service restart!\n      </li>\n      <li><strong>AlwaysInstallElevated:</strong> When the registry keys <code>AlwaysInstallElevated</code> in both <code>HKCU</code> and <code>HKLM</code> under <code>Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer</code> are set to 1, any unprivileged user can install an MSI package that executes with full elevated SYSTEM privileges!</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Exam Rule on Privilege Escalation:</strong> <strong>GTFOBins</strong> documents Unix SUID/sudo bypasses. <strong>Unquoted Service Paths</strong> execute intermediary binaries due to unquoted spaces. <strong>AlwaysInstallElevated</strong> allows unprivileged users to run MSIs with SYSTEM rights.\n    </div>\n\n    \n    \n        <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-banner\">\n          <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-info\">\n            <span style=\"font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 8px;\">🎯</span>\n            <div>\n              <strong style=\"font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--text-heading);\">Test Your Mastery: Spread 14</strong>\n              <div style=\"font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted);\">Practice all 10 targeted exam questions (Q131–Q140) on Privilege Escalation: SUID & Service Paths.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button class=\"btn-tool btn-mcq\" onclick=\"window.openMCQForSpread(13)\" style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 6px 14px;\">Start Quiz (Q131–Q140) →</button>\n        </div>"
